The plugin never redistributes Claude Code. At install time it downloads the
Claude Code CLI from Anthropic's official release bucket
(https://downloads.claude.ai/claude-code-releases/) and verifies it against a
SHA256 taken from Anthropic's GPG-signed release manifest. Claude Code is
proprietary software governed by Anthropic's terms:
https://www.anthropic.com/legal/consumer-terms and
https://www.anthropic.com/legal/commercial-terms

Third-party components
----------------------

1. claude-guard, settings.json and the guard test cases from
   mygrexit/claude-unraid-manager (https://github.com/mygrexit/claude-unraid-manager)
   MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 mygrexit.
   Adapted in src/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/claude-code-unraid/policy/guard and
   tests/bats/guard.bats. The container-specific pieces (the `host` wrapper and
   `/host/boot`) were removed; Unraid-native rules were added.

2. tmux (https://github.com/tmux/tmux), ISC License, Copyright (c) Nicholas
   Marriott and contributors. The plugin fetches the unmodified Slackware 15.0
   package tmux-3.2a-x86_64-1.txz from an official Slackware mirror at install
   time, verifies its SHA256 (CI verified the package signature against the
   Slackware Linux Project key), and extracts only usr/bin/tmux into the plugin's
   own directory. The package is not redistributed with the plugin.

3. The Unraid plugin manager script `plugin` from unraid/webgui
   (emhttp/plugins/dynamix.plugin.manager/scripts/plugin),
   Copyright 2005-2025 Lime Technology, GPLv2 only.
   A copy is vendored under tests/vendor/ for the test suite only. It is never
   shipped in the plugin package.
